Table`, `_ITM_registerTMCloneTable`,\n  `__cxa_finalize@GLIBC_2.2.5`, `__gmon_start__` (all `w`).\n* Rust: the same four, plus `__cxa_thread_atexit_impl`, `gettid`, `statx` (all `w`).\n\n## Undefined symbols in the Rust `.so` (must all be libc / libgcc)\n\n`nm -D --undefined-only` on the Rust `.so` reports only symbols provided by the\nplatform C library and by libgcc's unwinder:\n\n* libc: `printf`, `puts`, `strlen`, `memcpy`, `memmove`, `memset`, `bcmp`,\n  `malloc`, `calloc`, `realloc`, `free`, `posix_memalign`, `abort`,\n  `__errno_location`, `open64`, `close`, `read`, `write`, `writev`, `lseek64`,\n  `stat64`, `fstat64`, `mmap64`, `munmap`, `getcwd`, `getenv`, `readlink`,\n  `realpath`, `syscall`, `dl_iterate_phdr`, `__tls_get_addr`,\n  `pthread_key_create`, `pthread_key_delete`, `pthread_setspecific`.\n* libgcc (`libgcc_s.so.1`): `_Unwind_*`.\n\n`ldd` confirms the only shared-object dependencies are `libc.so.6`,\n`libgcc_s.so.1`, `linux-vdso.so.1` and the loader.\n\n**0 missing / 0 non-libc undefined symbols.**\n\n## Note on `printf` → `puts`\n\nBoth objects import `puts` as well as `printf`: GCC and LLVM both rewrite\n`printf(\"literal\\n\")` into `puts(\"literal\")`. This is a pure code-generation\ndetail — `puts` and `printf` write to the same `stdout` `FILE` stream, so the\nbytes and the buffering behaviour observed by a caller are unchanged. The\ndifferential tests compare the actual bytes on fd 1, which pins this down.\n\n## Feature combinations\n\n`translation/Cargo.toml` declares **no** `[features]` table, so the only feature\ncombination is the (empty) default one. `--no-default-features` and\n`--all-features` therefore select the same code, and both are still exercised by\n`run_all.sh` for completeness.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1749,"cache_read_input_tokens":27295,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1749,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_to