{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zykhcv6k4axs2y64a5lstamhjsigeabi446iyhc7ht7t3d2bjr3q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01YBfNSD9cGwNMULGGEkw6RN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"translation/CONFIGS.md","content":"# CONFIGS.md — Phase B configuration-surface table\n\n## Axes, derived from the branches `c_src/src/slicing.c` actually takes\n\nThe public surface is a single entry point, `slice()`; `slicing.h` exposes no\noptions struct, no init/teardown, and no flags, so the \"runtime options\" of this\nlibrary are encoded entirely in **which pointer arguments are null** and in the\n**shape of the data**. Every axis below is a branch or an index computation that\nreally exists in the C:\n\n| axis | values | where the C branches on it |\n|------|--------|-----------------------------|\n| **P** pointer mode (the library's only \"option flags\") | `NN` = both null, `SN` = start only, `NS` = stop only, `SS` = both given | `if (start_ptr)` L43, `if (stop_ptr)` L53 |\n| **L** string length class | `0`, `1`, small (2–16), medium (17–512), large (> `BUFSIZ` 4096), huge (1 MiB) | `strlen` L38 feeds every bound check; > `BUFSIZ` crosses stdio's buffer refill so it probes the write path, not just the arithmetic |\n| **D** byte content | ASCII, `printf` conversion bait (`%s %n %d %%`), high bytes `0x80–0xFF` / invalid UTF-8, whitespace + embedded `\\n`/`\\t`/`\\r`, every byte value `0x01–0xFF` in sequence | `%.*s` at L67 copies raw bytes; data is an argument, never a format |\n| **S** `*start_ptr` position | `0`, `1`, random interior, `L-1`, `L` (top boundary — **valid**, yields an empty slice) | `start > len` L45, pointer arithmetic `mystr + start` L67 |\n| **T** `*stop_ptr` position | `start+1` (minimum legal), random interior, `L-1`, `L` (top boundary) | `stop > len` L55, `stop <= start` L59, precision `stop - start` L67 |\n| **C** call composition | one call; a long sequence of calls whose *concatenated* stdout is compared | pins stdio buffering/flush interleaving across the whole pipeline, invisible to single-call tests |\n\nRows are the cross-product **pruned to the combinations the code distinguishes**:\nevery pointer mode against every length class, then every boundary position of\neach bound within the modes that read it, then each content class, then\ncomposition. Every row asserts (a) equal return value and (b) **byte-identical\nstdout** captured off fd 1 from both `.so`s.\n\nRandomization: each row runs `N` pseudo-random cases (`N` = 64–256 depending on\nrow cost) from a fixed-seed SplitMix64 PRNG (`seed = 0x5163_1EDA_7EA5_1CE5`), so\nruns are reproducible; lengths, byte values and in-range bound positions are all\ndrawn randomly inside the row's class.\n\n| #  | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|----|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1  | `slice` | **P=NN** (`start_ptr=NULL`, `stop_ptr=NULL`), **L=0** — empty string, whole-string default path, `stop = len = 0` ⇒ precision 0 | [x] |\n| 2  | `slice` | **P=NN**, **L=1**, random single byte `0x01–0xFF` | [x] |\n| 3  | `slice` | **P=NN**, **L=small (2–16)**, random ASCII | [x] |\n| 4  | `slice` | **P=NN**, **L=medium (17–512)**, random ASCII | [x] |\n| 5  | `slice` | **P=NN**, **L=large (4097–9000, > `BUFSIZ`)**, random ASCII | [x] |\n| 6  | `slice` | **P=NN**, **D=high bytes / invalid UTF-8** (`0x80–0xFF`, lone continuation bytes, truncated multi-byte sequences) | [x] |\n| 7  | `slice` | **P=NN**, **D=`printf` conversion bait** (`%s`, `%n`, `%d`, `%%`, `%1000000f`) embedded in the data | [x] |\n| 8  | `slice` | **P=NN**, **D=every byte value `0x01–0xFF` in order** (255-byte string), plus `\\n`/`\\t`/`\\r`-heavy strings | [x] |\n| 9  | `slice` | **P=NN**, **L=huge (1 MiB)** — oversized input, single call | [x] |\n| 10 | `slice` | **P=NN**, **C=sequence**: 200 random calls, concatenated stdout compared as one blob (stdio buffering) | [x] |\n| 11 | `slice` | **P=SN** (start given, `stop_ptr=NULL`), **L=0**, `*start=0` (only legal value) | [x] |\n| 12 | `slice` | **P=SN**, `*start=0` — suffix from the head, random `L` across all classes | [x] |\n| 13 | `slice` | **P=SN**, `*start=L` — **top boundary, valid**: `stop-start == 0`, prints just `\\n` | [x] |\n| 14 | `slice` | **P=SN**, `*start=L-1` — last byte only | [x] |\n| 15 | `slice` | **P=SN**, `*start` random in `[0, L]`, random `L` (small/medium) | [x] |\n| 16 | `slice` | **P=SN**, `*start` random in `[0, L]`, **L=large (> `BUFSIZ`)** | [x] |\n| 17 | `slice` | **P=SN**, `*start` random, **D=high bytes / invalid UTF-8** (slice may split a multi-byte sequence) | [x] |\n| 18 | `slice` | **P=NS** (`start_ptr=NULL` ⇒ `start=0`, stop given), `*stop=L` — full string via explicit stop | [x] |\n| 19 | `slice` | **P=NS**, `*stop=1` — minimum legal stop when `start=0` | [x] |\n| 20 | `slice` | **P=NS**, `*stop` random in `[1, L]`, random `L` (small/medium) | [x] |\n| 21 | `slice` | **P=NS**, `*stop` random in `[1, L]`, **L=large (> `BUFSIZ`)** and **L=huge (1 MiB)** | [x] |\n| 22 | `slice` | **P=NS**, `*stop` random, **D=high bytes + conversion bait** | [x] |\n| 23 | `slice` | **P=SS** (both given), `*start=0`, `*stop=L` — full window, both bounds explicit | [x] |\n| 24 | `slice` | **P=SS**, `*start=0`, `*stop=1` — minimal window at the head | [x] |\n| 25 | `slice` | **P=SS**, `*start=L-1`, `*stop=L` — minimal window at the tail (top boundary) | [x] |\n| 26 | `slice` | **P=SS**, random `0 <= start < stop <= L`, random `L` (small/medium) | [x] |\n| 27 | `slice` | **P=SS**, random window, **L=large (> `BUFSIZ`)** | [x] |\n| 28 | `slice` | **P=SS**, random window, **L=huge (1 MiB)** — window straddling many stdio buffer boundaries | [x] |\n| 29 | `slice` | **P=SS**, random window, **D=high bytes / invalid UTF-8** | [x] |\n| 30 | `slice` | **P=SS**, random window, **D=`printf` conversion bait** | [x] |\n| 31 | `slice` | **P=SS**, random window, **D